`haskell.py` emits an unresolved call as `haskell:<hint or external>:0-0:
<name>:function`, and the hint came only from a QUALIFIED import alias. The
`external` sentinel is deliberate -- its own comment says it exists so the
tagger uses unfiltered short-name matching -- but `gate_named_entry` ends:

    if ambiguous_names and name in ambiguous_names:
        return None

so with no module hint an AMBIGUOUS name reaches nothing while an unambiguous
one still matches. The servant baseline shows the split in one table:
`Prelude.putStrLn` classified with 8 chains and `Prelude.print` was ABSENT --
same module, same files, same bare call shape. That is the filed defect and its
own control.

SCOPE IS EXACTLY THAT ASYMMETRY, and narrower than the item implies. Only a
name in `ambiguous_names` is stamped -- 8 names (accept, connect, print, recv,
run, send, trace, yield), DERIVED from the catalogue rather than listed, so a
row added later is covered without editing this module. An unambiguous name
already classifies, so stamping it buys NOTHING and switches module filtering
on for a call that was working. That is this item's own cautionary case
(WI-lajus stamped too broadly, suppressed a permissive fallback and MOVED
VERDICTS THE WRONG WAY) applied in advance instead of after a regression;
`putStrLn`, `writeFile` and `getLine` are pinned by test to stay `external`.

TWO ROUTES COUNT AS EVIDENCE, everything else abstains:
  (a) an unqualified `import M (name)` list -- the route the item filed;
  (b) the name's HOME module being `Prelude` with nothing in the file claiming
      otherwise -- which is where the filed INSTANCE actually lives, since
      Haskell imports Prelude implicitly and it appears in no import line.
      The item's "module context lives in the IMPORT LIST" framing does not
      cover its own example.
A `qualified` import is skipped deliberately: it does not put the bare name in
scope, so a bare occurrence cannot have come from it. An explicit claim beats
the Prelude route, so `import Data.Text.IO (readFile)` beside
`import Prelude hiding (readFile)` never yields `Prelude`, and `hiding` with
no other claim abstains entirely.

