ALL THREE CHAINS READ BACK AGAINST SOURCE, AND THEY CORRECT THE RATIONALE.
The sites are servant-conduit:88/91, servant-pipes:90/93 and
servant-machines:82/85 -- the filing named TWO files, there are THREE. Each
carries `import Prelude ()` + `import Prelude.Compat`, the base-compat idiom,
whose EMPTY import list SUPPRESSES the implicit Prelude: `print` arrives
re-exported from `Prelude.Compat`, not from the implicit Prelude route (b)
reasons about. The stamp is still correct -- `Prelude.Compat` re-exports
`Prelude.print` verbatim, and the catalogue rows a function's HOME module
rather than whichever module re-exported it into a given file -- but the
justification encoded is not the one operating at these sites. Route (b) is
better read as "the home module is Prelude and nothing in this file claims
otherwise". Written into the docstring and pinned by two tests rather than
smoothed over, because it matters if the rule is ever widened.

